Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 09:17:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] crypto/internal/fips140deps/time: always use unbubbled
 monotonic clock

Backport CL 780540 to Go 1.26.

Use the system monotonic clock directly, rather than time.Since(start).
Avoids using the fake clock in synctest bubbles.

Inside a synctest bubble the fake clock makes every entropy sample
identical, so the SP 800-90B repetition count health test fails and
crypto/internal/fips140/drbg panics with "failed to obtain initial
entropy". This made net/http tests that use synctest (such as
TestClientConnReserveAndConsume) flaky when running with
GODEBUG=fips140=on.

Upstream CL: https://go.dev/cl/780540
Upstream commit: a81b20a431ce41417f7758929a2962d95a6a9453
Upstream issue: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/78557
---
 src/crypto/internal/fips140deps/time/time.go | 11 +++++++----
 src/crypto/rand/rand_test.go                 |  9 +++++++++
 src/runtime/time.go                          |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/crypto/internal/fips140deps/time/time.go b/src/crypto/internal/fips140deps/time/time.go
index eea37b772e4351ecdaf94c9c08ce31c35ce473a4..8e7aac61677418a65b1fced668241221fc420f4f 100644
--- a/src/crypto/internal/fips140deps/time/time.go
+++ b/src/crypto/internal/fips140deps/time/time.go
@@ -6,9 +6,9 @@
 
 package time
 
-import "time"
-
-var start = time.Now()
+import (
+	_ "unsafe"
+)
 
 // HighPrecisionNow returns a high-resolution timestamp suitable for measuring
 // small time differences. It uses the time package's monotonic clock.
@@ -17,5 +17,8 @@ var start = time.Now()
 // assumed to be sufficiently precise to measure time differences on the order
 // of tens to hundreds of nanoseconds.
 func HighPrecisionNow() int64 {
-	return int64(time.Since(start))
+	return monoTime()
 }
+
+//go:linkname monoTime
+func monoTime() int64
